module scADPLSignalDetection
module ddPCRQuantification
module qPCRQuantification
module fluorescenceImaging

manifest PBS
manifest PluronicF127
manifest MCPLysisBuffer
manifest MCF7_Cells
manifest SKOV3_Cells
manifest OVCAR3_Cells
manifest HEK293T_Cells
manifest MDA_MB_231_Cells
manifest PatientDerivedOrganoids
manifest CatBio_Probe
manifest FPBio_Probe
manifest StrepAvidin_OligoConjugate
manifest AntiBody_OligoConjugate
manifest SplintOligonucleotide
manifest LigationBuffer
manifest PreamplificationMix
manifest qPCR_MasterMix
manifest JW480_Inhibitor
manifest FITC_AntiCD45_Antibody
manifest RPhycoerythrin_Spike

// ============================================================
// Single-Cell Chemoproteomics Identifies Metastatic Activity
// Signatures in Breast Cancer
// Smitha Pillai, Laxton, Li, Lin, Karginova, Nanda, Olopade,
// Tay, Moellering - Sci. Adv. 10, eadp2622 (2024)
// DOI: 10.1126/sciadv.adp2622
//
// Platform: Single-Cell Activity-Dependent Proximity Ligation
// (scADPL) coupled to a valve-based push-up PDMS microfluidic
// chip with five chamber zones per assay unit:
//   I   Input fluid artery
//   II  Single-cell trapping chamber (8 um constriction)
//   III Cell lysis chamber (MCP lysis buffer)
//   IV  Proximity barcoding element incubation (whole proteome)
//   V   Proximity barcode ligation
// Output: barcoded amplicons retrieved off-chip by qPCR/ddPCR.
//
// This file encodes the full experimental pipeline:
//   PHASE 1  Single-plex validation (CTSL via ddPCR, NCEH1 via
//            qPCR) in SKOV3 cells.
//   PHASE 2  Multiplexed Ag-6 panel (NCEH1, MGLL, CTSL, FAAH,
//            CTSB, uPA) profiling with inhibitor specificity QC.
//   PHASE 3  Heterogeneity profiling across cell lines (HEK293T
//            vs SKOV3; SKOV3 vs OVCAR3).
//   PHASE 4  Patient-derived organoid (PDO) profiling from TNBC
//            primary and metastatic tumors, including ER+ within-
//            patient pleural effusion vs lymph node samples.
//
// CHEMICAL PROBES:
//   Cat-Bio (5 uM, 2 h, 37 C): cathepsin family-wide probe
//            targeting CTSL, CTSB (cysteine protease family).
//   FP-Bio (2 uM, 30 min, 37 C): serine hydrolase family-wide
//            probe targeting NCEH1, MGLL, FAAH, uPA.
//   Both probes applied simultaneously in multiplexed runs.
//
// DETECTION CHEMISTRY:
//   On-chip: streptavidin-oligo (SA-oligo) recognises biotin
//   tag on FP-Bio / Cat-Bio probe-protein complexes; antibody-
//   oligo conjugate (ab-oligo) recognises the target protein.
//   Proximity ligation: splint oligo bridges SA-oligo and
//   ab-oligo when probe-protein complex is formed; Ampligase
//   seals the nick (40 C, 45 min). Preamplification (18 cycles)
//   feeds into qPCR (Taqman, target-specific barcode channels)
//   or ddPCR (CTSL single-plex validation).
//   Spike-in control: R-phycoerythrin (RPE) added at lysis step
//   for inter-cell normalisation.
//
// KEY QUANTITATIVE PARAMETERS:
//   - sADPL sensitivity threshold: 10 pg whole proteome (36).
//   - Single HeLa cell protein content: ~2 ng (37).
//   - Average scADPL CTSL signal: 54-fold over vehicle control.
//   - Average scADPL NCEH1 signal: ~64-fold over vehicle control.
//   - Multiplexed reproducibility: Pearson r = 0.9981 (day1/day2).
//   - scADPL vs bulk sADPL correlation: Pearson r = 0.9288.
//   - JW480 (NCEH1 inhibitor, 2 uM): >90% NCEH1 signal inhibition;
//     no significant effect on other five targets.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main               -- device priming, probe labelling,
//                              single-plex CTSL validation (ddPCR),
//                              NCEH1 inhibitor specificity QC
//   BB2  ctslPass           -- ctslSignal > 0: probe-dependent CTSL
//                              barcodes detected; dispose
//   BB3  ctslFail           -- ctslSignal <= 0: no signal; drain
//   BB4  ctslJoin           -- join: NCEH1 branch begins
//   BB5  nceh1Pass          -- nceh1Signal > 0: valid NCEH1 signal
//                              and JW480 inhibition confirmed; dispose
//   BB6  nceh1Fail          -- nceh1Signal <= 0: no NCEH1 signal; drain
//   BB7  nceh1Join          -- join: Ag-6 multiplexed panel begins
//   BB8  multiplexPass      -- ag6Signal > 0: all six targets detected
//                              above background; dispose
//   BB9  multiplexFail      -- ag6Signal <= 0: multiplex failure; drain
//   BB10 multiplexJoin      -- join: cell-line heterogeneity profiling
//   BB11 heterogeneityPass  -- heteroSignal > 0: PCA clustering
//                              resolves SKOV3 vs OVCAR3; dispose
//   BB12 heterogeneityFail  -- heteroSignal <= 0: no separation; drain
//   BB13 heterogeneityJoin  -- join: PDO patient sample branch
//   BB14 pdoPass            -- pdoSignal > 0: metastatic Ag-6
//                              signature detected in PDOs; dispose
//   BB15 pdoFail            -- pdoSignal <= 0: no PDO signal; drain
//   BB16 finalCleanup       -- terminal: dispose all QC signals
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 - STEP 1: Prime microfluidic device.
//   2% Pluronics F-127 in PBS flowed through all channels
//   for 5 min to passivate PDMS surfaces and reduce non-
//   specific cell adhesion before cell loading.
//   Chip is a three-layer push-up PDMS valve device bonded
//   to glass (127.76 x 85.48 x 1 mm). Five chamber zones
//   per assay unit. SU-8-3025 photoresist features at 22 mm
//   and 70 mm heights; AZ40XT dome valve layer at 18 mm.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

primingPBS       = dispense 1 units of PBS
primingPluronic  = dispense 1 units of PluronicF127
primingMix       = mix primingPBS with primingPluronic for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 - STEP 2: Pulse-label SKOV3 cells with activity probes
//   off-chip prior to on-chip loading.
//   Cat-Bio: 5 uM, 2 h, 37 C in DMEM-F12 + 10% FBS.
//   FP-Bio:  2 uM, 30 min, 37 C in DMEM-F12 + 10% FBS.
//   Cells washed with PBS after labelling; resuspended in PBS
//   at 50,000-100,000 cells/mL for microfluidic loading.
//   NOTE: In PHASE 1, CTSL single-plex uses Cat-Bio only;
//         NCEH1 single-plex uses FP-Bio only. Both probes are
//         combined in PHASE 2 multiplexed runs.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

skov3Cells      = dispense 1 units of SKOV3_Cells
catBioProbe     = dispense 1 units of CatBio_Probe
fpBioProbe      = dispense 1 units of FPBio_Probe

// Cat-Bio labelling: 2 h at 37 C (= 120 min)
labelledCatBio  = mix skov3Cells with catBioProbe for 5s
heat labelledCatBio at 37c for 120m

// FP-Bio labelling: 30 min at 37 C
labelledFPBio   = mix skov3Cells with fpBioProbe for 5s
heat labelledFPBio at 37c for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 - STEP 3: Load probe-labelled SKOV3 cells on-chip.
//   Cells flow through input artery (I) into single-cell
//   trapping chamber (II) via hydrodynamic trapping.
//   NOTE: `mix` here abstracts a pressure-driven channel flow
//   event (single-cell capture), not DMF electrode mixing.
//   Each assay chamber captures exactly one cell per run.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rpeSpike             = dispense 1 units of RPhycoerythrin_Spike
trappedCatBioCell    = mix labelledCatBio with primingMix for 2s
trappedFPBioCell     = mix labelledFPBio with primingMix for 2s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 - STEP 4: On-chip cell lysis (Chamber III).
//   Cells lysed in MCP lysis buffer:
//   25 mM Tris pH 7.5, 150 mM NaCl, 1 mM EDTA, 1 mM EGTA,
//   0.5% Triton X-100, 0.5% sodium deoxycholate.
//   RPE spike-in control added at lysis step for each cell.
//   Whole-proteome lysate fills nanoliter dead volume of
//   chamber III; volume reduced vs bulk sADPL to maximise
//   sensitivity (working proteome concentration optimised
//   to match bulk sADPL window; fig. S2 in paper).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lysisBuffer          = dispense 1 units of MCPLysisBuffer
lysateCatBio         = mix trappedCatBioCell with lysisBuffer for 1m
lysateCatBio2        = mix lysateCatBio with rpeSpike for 5s

rpeSpike2            = dispense 1 units of RPhycoerythrin_Spike
lysateFPBio          = mix trappedFPBioCell with lysisBuffer for 1m
lysateFPBio2         = mix lysateFPBio with rpeSpike2 for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 - STEP 5: On-chip proximity barcoding (Chamber IV).
//   SA-oligo (4000 pM) recognises biotin tag on probe-protein
//   complex; ab-oligo (200 pM, target-specific) recognises
//   the protein epitope. Both recognition elements bind the
//   same probe-protein complex in nanoliter volume, bringing
//   the two oligos into proximity.
//   Incubation: 2 h at room temperature (25 C) on-chip.
//   Final concentrations mirror validated bulk sADPL window
//   (36) scaled to chip dead volume.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

saOligo              = dispense 1 units of StrepAvidin_OligoConjugate
abOligo              = dispense 1 units of AntiBody_OligoConjugate

barcodingReagents    = mix saOligo with abOligo for 5s
barcodedCatBio       = mix lysateCatBio2 with barcodingReagents for 2m
heat barcodedCatBio at 25c for 120m

saOligo2             = dispense 1 units of StrepAvidin_OligoConjugate
abOligo2             = dispense 1 units of AntiBody_OligoConjugate

barcodingReagents2   = mix saOligo2 with abOligo2 for 5s
barcodedFPBio        = mix lysateFPBio2 with barcodingReagents2 for 2m
heat barcodedFPBio at 25c for 120m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 - STEP 6: On-chip proximity ligation (Chamber V).
//   Splint oligonucleotide bridges SA-oligo and ab-oligo when
//   both are bound to the same probe-protein complex.
//   Ampligase (0.05 U) seals the nick under:
//     100 nM splint oligo, 0.3 mM NAD+, 10 mM DTT,
//     20 mM Tris-HCl pH 8.3, 50 mM KCl, 1.5 mM MgCl2.
//   Ligation: 40 C for 45 min (= 45 min).
//   Ligated barcoded amplicons are the quantifiable readout.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

splintOligo          = dispense 1 units of SplintOligonucleotide
ligBuf               = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer

ligationMixCat       = mix barcodedCatBio with splintOligo for 2s
ligationMixCat2      = mix ligationMixCat with ligBuf for 2s
heat ligationMixCat2 at 40c for 45m

splintOligo2         = dispense 1 units of SplintOligonucleotide
ligBuf2              = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer

ligationMixFP        = mix barcodedFPBio with splintOligo2 for 2s
ligationMixFP2       = mix ligationMixFP with ligBuf2 for 2s
heat ligationMixFP2 at 40c for 45m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 - STEP 7: Amplicon retrieval and preamplification.
//   Ligated product flushed out using 9 uL water off-chip.
//   Preamplification PCR (18 cycles):
//     2.5x buffer, 100 nM primers, 200 uM dNTPs,
//     9 U Phusion high-fidelity DNA polymerase.
//   NOTE: `mix` abstracts the off-chip flush and preamplification
//   step; the BioScript variable holds the preamplified product
//   ready for downstream quantification.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

preampMix            = dispense 1 units of PreamplificationMix
preamplifiedCatBio   = mix ligationMixCat2 with preampMix for 18m

preampMix2           = dispense 1 units of PreamplificationMix
preamplifiedFPBio    = mix ligationMixFP2 with preampMix2 for 18m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 - STEP 8: CTSL quantification by ddPCR.
//   ddPCR: 5 uL preamplified product into ddPCR reaction;
//   absolute quantification of barcoded amplicons (amplicons/uL).
//   Average signal: 54-fold above vehicle-only control.
//   (Fig. 1B in paper; n=2 independent biological replicates)
//   DETECTION: scADPLSignalDetection abstracts the ddPCR
//   instrument readout; ddPCRQuantification validates amplicon
//   count above noise threshold.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ctslSignal = detect ddPCRQuantification on preamplifiedCatBio for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: CTSL single-plex QC gate
// Pass (BB2): ctslSignal > 0 -> probe-dependent CTSL barcodes
//             detected above background (>54-fold expected).
// Fail (BB3): ctslSignal <= 0 -> no detectable amplicons;
//             likely probe labelling or ligation failure.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (ctslJoin).
// ============================================================

if (ctslSignal > 0) {
    dispose preamplifiedCatBio
} else {
    drain preamplifiedCatBio
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: ctslJoin
// Dispose CTSL QC signal. Control falls into NCEH1 branch.
// ============================================================

dispose ctslSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1 - STEP 9: NCEH1 specificity validation with JW480.
//   Parallel experiment: SKOV3 cells labelled with FP-Bio
//   then pre-treated with JW480 (2 uM, selective NCEH1
//   inhibitor) before on-chip processing.
//   Expected: JW480 inhibits NCEH1-specific scADPL signal
//   by >90% with no significant effect on other Ag-6 targets.
//   qPCR readout selected over ddPCR from this step forward:
//   higher SNR, amenable to multiplexing across target channels.
//   (Fig. 1C, Fig. 2B in paper)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

skov3CellsQC    = dispense 1 units of SKOV3_Cells
fpBioProbeQC    = dispense 1 units of FPBio_Probe
jw480           = dispense 1 units of JW480_Inhibitor

// Pre-treat with JW480 before FP-Bio labelling to confirm
// target-selective inhibition (2 uM JW480, 30 min, 37 C)
jw480Treated    = mix skov3CellsQC with jw480 for 5s
heat jw480Treated at 37c for 30m

// FP-Bio labelling post-inhibitor treatment
labelledQC      = mix jw480Treated with fpBioProbeQC for 5s
heat labelledQC at 37c for 30m

// On-chip: trap, lyse, barcode, ligate (same as STEP 3-6)
rpeSpike3       = dispense 1 units of RPhycoerythrin_Spike
primingMix2     = dispense 1 units of PBS
trappedQCCell   = mix labelledQC with primingMix2 for 2s

lysisBuffer2    = dispense 1 units of MCPLysisBuffer
lysateQC        = mix trappedQCCell with lysisBuffer2 for 1m
lysateQC2       = mix lysateQC with rpeSpike3 for 5s

saOligoQC       = dispense 1 units of StrepAvidin_OligoConjugate
abOligoQC       = dispense 1 units of AntiBody_OligoConjugate
barcodingQC     = mix saOligoQC with abOligoQC for 5s
barcodedQC      = mix lysateQC2 with barcodingQC for 2m
heat barcodedQC at 25c for 120m

splintQC        = dispense 1 units of SplintOligonucleotide
ligBufQC        = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer
ligationQC      = mix barcodedQC with splintQC for 2s
ligationQC2     = mix ligationQC with ligBufQC for 2s
heat ligationQC2 at 40c for 45m

preampQC        = dispense 1 units of PreamplificationMix
preamplifiedQC  = mix ligationQC2 with preampQC for 18m

// qPCR detection on NCEH1-specific barcode channel
// Expected: signal suppressed >90% vs no-inhibitor control
nceh1Signal = detect qPCRQuantification on preamplifiedQC for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: NCEH1 inhibitor specificity QC gate
// Pass (BB5): nceh1Signal > 0 -> residual signal present
//             (confirms partial probe labelling competed by
//             JW480); target specificity validated when compared
//             to uninhibited control. Dispose.
// Fail (BB6): nceh1Signal <= 0 -> no signal at all; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (nceh1Join).
// NOTE: A valid experiment expects nceh1Signal to be >90% lower
// than the uninhibited preamplifiedFPBio signal. The binary QC
// gate here checks for the presence of a processed product;
// the >90% inhibition fold-change comparison is performed
// off-chip by the qPCR instrument software.
// ============================================================

if (nceh1Signal > 0) {
    dispose preamplifiedQC
} else {
    drain preamplifiedQC
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: nceh1Join
// Dispose NCEH1 QC signal. Control falls into Ag-6 multiplexed
// panel branch (BB8/BB9).
// ============================================================

dispose nceh1Signal

// ============================================================
// PHASE 2: Multiplexed Ag-6 Panel in SKOV3 Single Cells
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2 - STEP 1: Pulse-label SKOV3 cells with both probes
//   simultaneously.
//   Cat-Bio 5 uM (2 h, 37 C) + FP-Bio 2 uM (30 min, 37 C)
//   applied to same cells for dual-probe multiplexing.
//   FP-Bio labels NCEH1, MGLL, FAAH, uPA (serine hydrolases).
//   Cat-Bio labels CTSL, CTSB (cathepsin family).
//   Six orthogonal barcode channels enable simultaneous
//   qPCR quantification from the same single-cell lysate.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

skov3Ag6        = dispense 1 units of SKOV3_Cells
catBioAg6       = dispense 1 units of CatBio_Probe
fpBioAg6        = dispense 1 units of FPBio_Probe

// Sequential labelling: FP-Bio first (30 min), then Cat-Bio
// added to ongoing FP-Bio incubation for remaining 90 min
// such that both probes are present for the final 30 min.
// Simplified here as sequential mix operations.
labelledFP_Ag6  = mix skov3Ag6 with fpBioAg6 for 5s
heat labelledFP_Ag6 at 37c for 30m

labelledDual    = mix labelledFP_Ag6 with catBioAg6 for 5s
heat labelledDual at 37c for 90m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2 - STEP 2: Single-cell capture, lysis, and barcoding.
//   Cells resuspended to 50,000-100,000 cells/mL in PBS.
//   Loaded onto chip; single cells trapped per assay chamber.
//   MCP lysis buffer + RPE spike-in at Chamber III.
//   SA-oligo (4000 pM) and ab-oligo cocktail (200 pM each,
//   six antibody-oligo conjugates for six Ag-6 targets)
//   added to whole-proteome lysate in Chamber IV.
//   Incubation 2 h at 25 C; ligation 45 min at 40 C.
//   NOTE: n = 8 single cells profiled per condition (Fig. 2A).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rpeAg6          = dispense 1 units of RPhycoerythrin_Spike
primingAg6      = dispense 1 units of PBS
trappedAg6Cell  = mix labelledDual with primingAg6 for 2s

lysisAg6        = dispense 1 units of MCPLysisBuffer
lysateAg6       = mix trappedAg6Cell with lysisAg6 for 1m
lysateAg6b      = mix lysateAg6 with rpeAg6 for 5s

saAg6           = dispense 1 units of StrepAvidin_OligoConjugate
abAg6           = dispense 1 units of AntiBody_OligoConjugate
barcodingAg6    = mix saAg6 with abAg6 for 5s
barcodedAg6     = mix lysateAg6b with barcodingAg6 for 2m
heat barcodedAg6 at 25c for 120m

splintAg6       = dispense 1 units of SplintOligonucleotide
ligAg6          = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer
ligMixAg6       = mix barcodedAg6 with splintAg6 for 2s
ligMixAg6b      = mix ligMixAg6 with ligAg6 for 2s
heat ligMixAg6b at 40c for 45m

preampAg6       = dispense 1 units of PreamplificationMix
preamplifiedAg6 = mix ligMixAg6b with preampAg6 for 18m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2 - STEP 3: Multiplexed qPCR quantification (Ag-6).
//   Six orthogonal Taqman barcode channels simultaneously
//   quantified on CFX384 Real-Time System (384-well plates).
//   0.9 uM primers + 0.45 uM Taqman probe per channel in
//   Luna Universal Probe qPCR Master Mix.
//   Values normalised to RPE spike-in control per cell.
//   Expected fold-changes vs no-probe DMSO control (Fig. 2A):
//     NCEH1: >20-fold, MGLL: >20-fold, CTSL: >20-fold
//     FAAH: detectable, CTSB: detectable, uPA: detectable
// ------------------------------------------------------------

qpcrMix         = dispense 1 units of qPCR_MasterMix
ag6WithQPCR     = mix preamplifiedAg6 with qpcrMix for 2s
ag6Signal       = detect qPCRQuantification on ag6WithQPCR for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Ag-6 multiplexed panel QC gate
// Pass (BB8): ag6Signal > 0 -> all six target barcode channels
//             detected above no-probe background; dispose.
// Fail (BB9): ag6Signal <= 0 -> multiplex failure (ligation
//             or preamplification failure); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (multiplexJoin).
// ============================================================

if (ag6Signal > 0) {
    dispose ag6WithQPCR
} else {
    drain ag6WithQPCR
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: multiplexJoin
// Dispose Ag-6 QC signal. Control falls into heterogeneity
// profiling branch (BB11/BB12).
// ============================================================

dispose ag6Signal

// ============================================================
// PHASE 3: Heterogeneity Profiling Across Cell Lines
// (HEK293T vs SKOV3; SKOV3 vs OVCAR3)
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 3 - STEP 1: Prepare and label HEK293T and OVCAR3 cells.
//   HEK293T: non-cancer kidney control (tissue-type mismatch
//            comparison vs SKOV3 ovarian cancer; Fig. 3A).
//   OVCAR3:  low-aggressiveness ovarian cancer (tissue-matched
//            comparison vs SKOV3 high-aggressiveness; Fig. 3B).
//   Both cell lines dual-probe labelled identically to PHASE 2.
//   n > 10 isolated single cells per target per cell line.
//   Activity normalised to HEK293T (Fig. 3A) or OVCAR3 (Fig. 3B)
//   as respective internal reference populations.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

hek293t         = dispense 1 units of HEK293T_Cells
ovcar3          = dispense 1 units of OVCAR3_Cells

catBioHetero    = dispense 1 units of CatBio_Probe
fpBioHetero     = dispense 1 units of FPBio_Probe

// Label HEK293T cells
labelledHEK_FP  = mix hek293t with fpBioHetero for 5s
heat labelledHEK_FP at 37c for 30m

catBioH2        = dispense 1 units of CatBio_Probe
labelledHEK     = mix labelledHEK_FP with catBioH2 for 5s
heat labelledHEK at 37c for 90m

// Label OVCAR3 cells
fpBioO          = dispense 1 units of FPBio_Probe
labelledOVC_FP  = mix ovcar3 with fpBioO for 5s
heat labelledOVC_FP at 37c for 30m

catBioO         = dispense 1 units of CatBio_Probe
labelledOVC     = mix labelledOVC_FP with catBioO for 5s
heat labelledOVC at 37c for 90m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 3 - STEP 2: On-chip scADPL for both control cell lines.
//   Same chamber-by-chamber workflow as PHASE 2.
//   HEK293T and OVCAR3 processed on separate chip runs.
//   Each cell trapped, lysed, barcoded, and ligated individually.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// HEK293T on-chip processing
rpeHEK          = dispense 1 units of RPhycoerythrin_Spike
primHEK         = dispense 1 units of PBS
trappedHEK      = mix labelledHEK with primHEK for 2s

lysHEK          = dispense 1 units of MCPLysisBuffer
lysateHEK       = mix trappedHEK with lysHEK for 1m
lysateHEKb      = mix lysateHEK with rpeHEK for 5s

saHEK           = dispense 1 units of StrepAvidin_OligoConjugate
abHEK           = dispense 1 units of AntiBody_OligoConjugate
barcodeHEK      = mix saHEK with abHEK for 5s
barcodedHEK     = mix lysateHEKb with barcodeHEK for 2m
heat barcodedHEK at 25c for 120m

splintHEK       = dispense 1 units of SplintOligonucleotide
ligHEK          = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer
ligMixHEK       = mix barcodedHEK with splintHEK for 2s
ligMixHEKb      = mix ligMixHEK with ligHEK for 2s
heat ligMixHEKb at 40c for 45m

preampHEK       = dispense 1 units of PreamplificationMix
preamplHEK      = mix ligMixHEKb with preampHEK for 18m

// OVCAR3 on-chip processing
rpeOVC          = dispense 1 units of RPhycoerythrin_Spike
primOVC         = dispense 1 units of PBS
trappedOVC      = mix labelledOVC with primOVC for 2s

lysOVC          = dispense 1 units of MCPLysisBuffer
lysateOVC       = mix trappedOVC with lysOVC for 1m
lysateOVCb      = mix lysateOVC with rpeOVC for 5s

saOVC           = dispense 1 units of StrepAvidin_OligoConjugate
abOVC           = dispense 1 units of AntiBody_OligoConjugate
barcodeOVC      = mix saOVC with abOVC for 5s
barcodedOVC     = mix lysateOVCb with barcodeOVC for 2m
heat barcodedOVC at 25c for 120m

splintOVC       = dispense 1 units of SplintOligonucleotide
ligOVC          = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer
ligMixOVC       = mix barcodedOVC with splintOVC for 2s
ligMixOVCb      = mix ligMixOVC with ligOVC for 2s
heat ligMixOVCb at 40c for 45m

preampOVC       = dispense 1 units of PreamplificationMix
preamplOVC      = mix ligMixOVCb with preampOVC for 18m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 3 - STEP 3: qPCR and fluorescence imaging readout.
//   qPCRQuantification: six-channel Ag-6 qPCR on each cell line.
//   fluorescenceImaging: abstracts PCA dimensional reduction
//   and heatmap visualisation of Z-score activity profiles
//   across single cells (Fig. 3D/E/F in paper).
//   Key finding: SKOV3 significantly higher Ag-6 activity vs
//   both HEK293T (all six targets, p <= 0.0001-0.03) and
//   OVCAR3 (five of six targets significant, Fig. 3B).
//   PCA separates SKOV3 vs OVCAR3 at PC1 = 84.67%.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

qpcrHEK         = dispense 1 units of qPCR_MasterMix
hekWithQPCR     = mix preamplHEK with qpcrHEK for 2s

qpcrOVC         = dispense 1 units of qPCR_MasterMix
ovcWithQPCR     = mix preamplOVC with qpcrOVC for 2s

heteroSignal    = detect fluorescenceImaging on hekWithQPCR for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB11 / BB12: Cell-line heterogeneity QC gate
// Pass (BB11): heteroSignal > 0 -> significant Ag-6 activity
//              difference between SKOV3 and control lines
//              resolved; PCA clustering validates; dispose.
// Fail (BB12): heteroSignal <= 0 -> no measurable difference;
//              drain.
// Both branches converge at BB13 (heterogeneityJoin).
// ============================================================

if (heteroSignal > 0) {
    dispose hekWithQPCR
    dispose ovcWithQPCR
} else {
    drain hekWithQPCR
    drain ovcWithQPCR
}

// ============================================================
// BB13: heterogeneityJoin
// Dispose heterogeneity QC signal. Control falls into PDO
// patient sample branch (BB14/BB15).
// ============================================================

dispose heteroSignal

// ============================================================
// PHASE 4: Patient-Derived Organoid (PDO) Profiling
// Samples: TNBC between-patient (PDO1-PDO6) and ER+ within-
// patient (pleural effusion L/R, lymph node metastasis).
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 4 - STEP 1: PDO preparation.
//   Fresh core needle biopsies enzymatically digested 1 h to
//   generate cell suspension. Pleural effusion cells collected
//   by centrifugation at 450g for 10 min.
//   Cells mixed with Matrigel (MG), plated in 24-well plates,
//   solidified at 37 C. BC PDO media supplemented.
//   PDOs cultured to 50-100 mm diameter before dissociation.
//   Dissociation: Dispase 37 C 20 min; TrypLE 37 C 5-10 min.
//   Final suspension: 500 uL BC PDO media, kept on ice.
//   ANTI-CD45 staining: cells labelled with FITC-anti-CD45
//   (30 min on ice) to identify and exclude immune cells
//   during on-chip imaging, preventing contamination of
//   tumour-cell activity signatures. (fig. S6 in paper)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pdoSuspension   = dispense 1 units of PatientDerivedOrganoids
fitcAntiCD45    = dispense 1 units of FITC_AntiCD45_Antibody
stainedPDO      = mix pdoSuspension with fitcAntiCD45 for 30m

// CD45 staining on ice (4 C = cold approximation at 4c)
heat stainedPDO at 4c for 30m

// Probe labelling of PDO single-cell suspension
catBioPDO       = dispense 1 units of CatBio_Probe
fpBioPDO        = dispense 1 units of FPBio_Probe

labelledPDO_FP  = mix stainedPDO with fpBioPDO for 5s
heat labelledPDO_FP at 37c for 30m

labelledPDO     = mix labelledPDO_FP with catBioPDO for 5s
heat labelledPDO at 37c for 90m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 4 - STEP 2: On-chip scADPL for PDO single cells.
//   CD45+ immune cells identified by on-chip fluorescence
//   imaging (FITC channel) and excluded from scADPL analysis.
//   Only CD45- tumour cells proceed through lysis and barcoding.
//   NOTE: `detect fluorescenceImaging` at trapping step
//   abstracts the brightfield + FITC fluorescence screen used
//   to confirm single tumour cell capture per chamber.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

rpePDO          = dispense 1 units of RPhycoerythrin_Spike
primPDO         = dispense 1 units of PBS
trappedPDO      = mix labelledPDO with primPDO for 2s

// On-chip CD45 imaging QC: confirm FITC-negative (tumour) cell
pdoTumourSignal = detect fluorescenceImaging on trappedPDO for 10s

lysPDO          = dispense 1 units of MCPLysisBuffer
lysatePDO       = mix trappedPDO with lysPDO for 1m
lysatePDOb      = mix lysatePDO with rpePDO for 5s

saPDO           = dispense 1 units of StrepAvidin_OligoConjugate
abPDO           = dispense 1 units of AntiBody_OligoConjugate
barcodePDO      = mix saPDO with abPDO for 5s
barcodedPDO     = mix lysatePDOb with barcodePDO for 2m
heat barcodedPDO at 25c for 120m

splintPDO       = dispense 1 units of SplintOligonucleotide
ligPDO          = dispense 1 units of LigationBuffer
ligMixPDO       = mix barcodedPDO with splintPDO for 2s
ligMixPDOb      = mix ligMixPDO with ligPDO for 2s
heat ligMixPDOb at 40c for 45m

preampPDO       = dispense 1 units of PreamplificationMix
preamplPDO      = mix ligMixPDOb with preampPDO for 18m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 4 - STEP 3: qPCR Ag-6 quantification on PDO cells.
//   Values normalised to RPE spike-in and within each target
//   to PDO1 (primary tumour reference) for TNBC samples, or
//   to Lymph met for ER+ within-patient samples.
//   Key finding: Ag-6 activity highest in metastatic vs
//   primary tumour PDOs; peak in liver metastases (PDO3/PDO4).
//   scADPL vs bulk sADPL concordance confirmed in ER+ patient
//   pleural effusion and lymph node samples (Fig. 4D/E).
//   scADPL resolves intra-tumour single-cell heterogeneity
//   not visible in bulk organoid measurements.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

qpcrPDO         = dispense 1 units of qPCR_MasterMix
pdoWithQPCR     = mix preamplPDO with qpcrPDO for 2s
pdoSignal       = detect qPCRQuantification on pdoWithQPCR for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB14 / BB15: PDO patient sample QC gate
// Pass (BB14): pdoSignal > 0 -> Ag-6 barcoded amplicons
//              detected in PDO single cells; metastatic activity
//              signature confirmed; dispose.
// Fail (BB15): pdoSignal <= 0 -> no amplicons (PDO preparation
//              or probe labelling failure); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB16 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (pdoSignal > 0) {
    dispose pdoWithQPCR
    dispose pdoTumourSignal
} else {
    drain pdoWithQPCR
    drain pdoTumourSignal
}

// ============================================================
// BB16: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all remaining QC signal droplets.
// Experiment ends. Results: Ag-6 enzyme panel activity
// increases with metastatic potential across BC cell lines
// and patient-derived organoids; scADPL resolves single-cell
// heterogeneity invisible to bulk proteomic methods.
// ============================================================

dispose pdoSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
